      "checkpoint": {
        "version": 1,
        "goals": [
          {
            "text": "Fix missing pytest marks on a class inheriting from two base classes each with a distinct @pytest.mark, so both inherited markers are collected instead of only the first per MRO.",
            "sourceIds": [
              "01a0e6bf-0f1c-7136-8a3f-2c6f10b1667a",
              "01a0e6bf-4ad2-76af-928a-b5a689c6be97"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Fix the TypeError introduced by MRO-merging in get_unpacked_marks by making the dedup key hashable (kwargs is an unhashable dict).",
            "sourceIds": [
              "01a0e6c1-9f1d-707b-8b96-e52ad8b951b7",
              "01a0e6c1-9f27-77cc-8b0d-5263bb76acdb"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "facts": [
          {
            "text": "Bug: a class inheriting from two base classes Foo and Bar, each with a distinct @pytest.mark, loses one marker because pytestmark is resolved via MRO (last wins).",
            "sourceIds": [
              "01a0e6bf-0f1c-7136-8a3f-2c6f10b1667a",
              "01a0e6c0-7aed-7128-aae5-f5daa3854be7"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "get_unpacked_marks() reads obj.pytestmark via getattr (follows MRO, collapses overlapping base marks) and populates own_markers; Mark is unhashable (kwargs is a dict).",
            "sourceIds": [
              "01a0e6bf-4adf-766d-94b3-ed0857a35e63",
              "01a0e6bf-746d-75a3-818a-09288955c826",
              "01a0e6c1-89c5-7119-9900-85adb2ddb74a"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Real pytest collection of TestDings(Foo, Bar) exposed only the foo mark; -m bar selected nothing, confirming the bug.",
            "sourceIds": [
              "01a0e6c0-7aed-7128-aae5-f5daa3854be7",
              "01a0e6c0-9176-751a-8a61-82f5e7590c01"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Existing tests test_mark_decorator_baseclasses_merged and test_mark_decorator_subclass_does_not_propagate_to_base must not be broken by the fix.",
            "sourceIds": [
              "01a0e6c0-9180-72ce-b812-4d2742e6d7b9",
              "01a0e6c0-b6e1-76a8-99c3-b04e2786feda"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "changedPaths": [
          {
            "text": "Proposed to modify get_unpacked_marks() in src/_pytest/mark/structures.py to merge marks across the object's MRO with a hashable dedup key. The edit was applied to the workspace file but never saved to disk.",
            "sourceIds": [
              "01a0e6c1-4960-77d9-93cb-f493d2fa8252",
              "01a0e6c1-528c-74de-8605-5645d8cf5a6e"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "tests": [
          {
            "text": "Reproduction collected TestDings::test_dings; with the unsaved MRO-merging edit it then raised TypeError: unhashable type: 'dict' during collection.",
            "target": "test_markers_check2.py (external /tmp/repro)",
            "revision": null,
            "outcome": "failed",
            "sourceIds": [
              "01a0e6c1-89c5-7119-9900-85adb2ddb74a",
              "01a0e6c2-e97d-73dd-81cd-83473f823155"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Assertion-based reproduction (TestDings(Foo, Bar) with foo/bar marks) failed because TestDings.pytestmark returned only ['foo']; the bar assertion failed.",
            "target": "test_markers_check.py (external /tmp/repro)",
            "revision": null,
            "outcome": "failed",
            "sourceIds": [
              "01a0e6c0-2232-73bc-8ccd-46633c0d782b"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "unfinished": [
          {
            "text": "No fix was implemented or saved. get_unpacked_marks() still uses the original MRO-collapsing implementation, and the reproduction only confirms the bug.",
            "sourceIds": [
              "01a0e6bf-746d-75a3-818a-09288955c826",
              "01a0e6c1-4960-77d9-93cb-f493d2fa8252"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A real fix and a focused regression test in the pytest suite remain, plus a deduplication key that works for unhashable Mark objects (e.g. sorted kwargs items).",
            "sourceIds": [
              "01a0e6bf-881e-707d-b38c-39eb4ea84ca5",
              "01a0e6c1-9f1d-707b-8b96-e52ad8b951b7"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "uncertainties": [
          {
            "text": "Whether merging marks across the MRO in get_unpacked_marks() is the minimal, correct fix, or whether it risks marker duplication/ordering regressions for existing tests.",
            "sourceIds": [
              "01a0e6bf-746d-75a3-818a-09288955c826",
              "01a0e6c0-9180-72ce-b812-4d2742e6d7b9"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Whether the intended fix should also change own_markers population in python.py or only get_unpacked_marks().",
